{"duration": 58.357, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "An archivist lifts a dusty notebook, winces as a faint glow flickers.", "start": 0.08, "end": 4.057}, {"beat": 0, "text": "Her colleagues laugh, saying the old papers are just ink stains.", "start": 4.277, "end": 7.529}, {"beat": 1, "text": "She places the notebook on a metal tray.", "start": 7.949, "end": 9.964}, {"beat": 1, "text": "A soft hiss escapes, invisible particles slipping out.", "start": 10.184, "end": 13.088}, {"beat": 2, "text": "She slides the tray into a lead\u2011lined box.", "start": 13.508, "end": 15.881}, {"beat": 2, "text": "The lid clangs, sealing the hiss inside.", "start": 16.101, "end": 18.242}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it\u2019s like holding a candle in rain\u2014without protection flame dies.", "start": 18.662, "end": 22.641}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Curie's 1890s papers still contain radium\u2011226, whose half\u2011life is about 1,600 years.", "start": 23.061, "end": 30.631}, {"beat": 4, "text": "That makes the notebooks radioactive for well over a thousand years.", "start": 30.851, "end": 34.46}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Lead blocks the penetrating radiation, keeping the lab safe.", "start": 34.68, "end": 37.904}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Anyone who wants to read them must wear protective clothing.", "start": 38.124, "end": 41.252}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Ironically, the notebooks that birthed radioactivity are now the most guarded artifacts.", "start": 41.672, "end": 46.756}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Even her cookbooks glow with the same deadly ink.", "start": 46.976, "end": 49.339}, {"beat": 6, "text": "Researchers don gloves, goggles, and thick lead aprons before opening a box.", "start": 49.759, "end": 54.239}, {"beat": 6, "text": "The air in the vault is monitored for stray particles.", "start": 54.459, "end": 57.237}], "words": [{"w": "An", "start": 0.145, "end": 0.195, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "archivist", "start": 0.245, "end": 0.82, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"